			<item>
				<title>Running Uptime Kuma on my old phone</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/uptime-kuma-termux/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 21 Nov 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/uptime-kuma-termux/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;how-i-ran-uptime-kuma-on-termux-with-cloudflare-tunnels&#34;&gt;How I ran uptime-kuma on termux with cloudflare tunnels&lt;a href=&#34;#how-i-ran-uptime-kuma-on-termux-with-cloudflare-tunnels&#34; class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;&lt;svg class=&#34;h-4 w-4&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34;&gt;&lt;g fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71&#34;/&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71&#34;/&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The project &lt;a&#xA;    href=&#34;github.com/louislam/uptime-kuma&#34;&gt;uptime-kuma&lt;/a&gt; is the first ever piece of software I have self hosted. Previously, I was scared  of self hosting because&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;I was not aware of what hardware requirements would be sufficient for my needs&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;What I even wanted to self host&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Domain names and IP Addresses (I don&amp;rsquo;t want to expose my home IP Address)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Through research, I found my answers&lt;/p&gt;</description>
